WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.356
- When you see regret in a man's
eyes, it's fucking painful.

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:06.939
(gentle music)

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.840
You should really go to
a retirement home one day

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.820
and volunteer and just talk to them.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.980
It will make you want to do
shit every minute of your life,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.510
because when you're 90,
and you're not mobile,

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.640
and you're tired, and it's
over, you can't do it.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.710
You can't do it.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.260
You can't build that company you wanted,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.240
you can't spend that time with your kid.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.778
It's regret.

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:28.611
- Yeah.

00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:30.440
- And it fucking drives
the shit out of me.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.273
How old are you?

00:00:31.273 --> 00:00:32.746
- I'm 27, 27.

00:00:32.746 --> 00:00:34.454
- You got fucking time.

00:00:34.454 --> 00:00:36.830
It's a balance of regret and patience.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.330
Like you can go hard for three years,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.700
do nothing right, wake
up, and be young as fuck.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.480
The amount of people who
are watching this right now,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.300
maybe even in this room,
that are sad, men and women,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.960
that they didn't go for it,
and didn't make the move,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.760
and didn't try, that regret
is a hell of a lot longer

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.000
and more painful, and more drawn out

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.800
than the instant
rejection of going for it.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.300
It's just the way it is.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.980
Even if you think of random, dumb stuff

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.120
like not asking out that
person in high school,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.650
the stuff lingers.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.160
It's the stuff that you
don't do that bothers you,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.130
and so for the purebred
entrepreneurs in here

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.390
that haven't decided to make that leap

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.890
or take that at-bat, I implore
you to do so right away

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.550
because this window closes, too.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.070
And the one thing that I ask you to do

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.636
is to not look back and regret

00:01:27.636 --> 00:01:28.583
that you wavered on the moment
that was available to you.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.490
I think your biggest
concern as you get older

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.270
is you wanna make sure you're
doing things for yourself,

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.870
not to make him proud,

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.020
and that's gonna be the
toughest thing for you.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.650
The biggest poison in us is regret.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.080
Everybody here is already sitting

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.970
with two, three, four things they can

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.700
think of very quickly that they regret.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.970
Right now, already, you
got a lot more life to go,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.410
and right now you feel okay because

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.640
you've got a lot of life to go.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.300
But if you spend time with
people in their 80s and 90s,

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.060
the thing they will absolutely
teach you if you really dig

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.780
is regret fucking sucks.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.640
Go talk to 90-year-olds.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.593
They regret.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.700
They talk about regret.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.810
I wish is the opening line.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.850
Go and volunteer in a nursing home,

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.450
because you're gonna see something

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.020
that you haven't seen
in such a pure state.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.580
You will face regret in a way

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.320
that will fuck with you so hard

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.720
that you will stay focused and on track

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.130
for the rest of your fucking life.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.570
The number one thing that you will taste

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.400
if you go to a nursing home

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.400
is you will find multiple people

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.420
that will talk to you about regrets

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.060
in a way that will pierce your soul

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.100
in a way that you've never felt before,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.450
because they're actually in that place

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.290
where time has run out.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.210
I just really think, I really believe

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.043
this from the bottom of my heart,

00:02:55.043 --> 00:02:56.774
I think we only live one time.

00:02:56.774 --> 00:02:59.920
And we don't act like it.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.756
I just really wish people
knew that they were gonna die.

00:03:03.756 --> 00:03:05.840
(audience laughs)

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.920
How can you not stay motivated?

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.310
Do you know that the odds of becoming

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.520
a human being are 400 trillion to one?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.462
You gonna remember this?

00:03:13.462 --> 00:03:14.295
(audience member coughs)

00:03:14.295 --> 00:03:15.570
- [Woman] I do.
- Good.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.243
One fucking life.

